{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would result in the loss of a family-sized dwellinghouse, the need for which is clearly demonstrated in the development plan and supporting evidence base. While it would provide a dwelling in the form of an HMO, it fails to demonstrate that this meets an identified need. Further, it would not present a suitable quality of accommodation specifically for an HMO.&nbsp;As such, the proposal is considered to have a detrimental impact on the borough&#39;s housing supply and is contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024)Policies D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies SP3,&nbsp; DMD1, and DMH5 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)East London HMO Guidance (4)",
    "The applicant has failed to present plans which accurately depict the HMO or the existing site. The submitted drawings conflict with the information contained in the HMO licence and the applicant’s correspondence, creating inconsistency and a lack of clarity over the HMO and occupancy levels. As a result, the proposed development cannot be accurately assessed, it cannot be demonstrated that it complies with:National Planning Policy Framework (MHCLG, December 2024)Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies&nbsp;SP2 and&nbsp;DMD1 of the Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September 2024)"
  ],
